    coverage_wrapper_undefined_identifier_clusters_2026-08-31, 1, "2026-11-03 (tr-cov lane): deferred - causes C/D/E/F need wrapper capture + native compile on Linux; blocked on coverage_wrapper_not_retained_keep_artifacts verification. Keep open."
    coverage_wrapper_undefined_identifier_clusters_2026-08-31, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: cluster matrix at tip - most doc clusters already dead; the LIVE clusters (expected/typed_return/omod Undef) were one defect: neither checker (seed Node::If binds let_pattern only in the statement arm; pure-Simple checker identical) binds if-val/elif-val patterns when the if is an EXPRESSION, so val x = if val t = opt: f(t) else: g() fails native compile with Undefined t while the interpreter resolves it. Fix (pure-Simple, behaviour-identical, 20 sites in 3 files): method_calls_literals.spl 9 sites, switch_operators_calls.spl 2 sites, expr_dispatch.spl 9 sites - converted to the statement form the checkers bind; effectful branches use if/else with dummy init so exactly one lowering/call is emitted. Verification: closure probes rc=0 (were 16-18 modules reporting); doc-named specs green (pmm 25/25, cell_format 18/18, linalg 2/2, handler_registry 4/4, lean, array_at_native 10/10); new spec if_val_expression_binding 4/4; neighbours builtin_method_table_sweep 23/23, declared_enum_constructor 16/16. Residuals: the checker fix itself is a compiler-lane item (seed cannot be patched in-lane; 59 = if val sites remain elsewhere in src/compiler as latent clusters); Dict cluster owner unidentified; artifact_manifest_spec 5/31 is a live DIFFERENT defect (ambiguous call owner-collision, needs its own lane). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/if_val_expression_binding_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/expr_dispatch.spl"

